-crimson","name":"Doctor Crimson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T13:59:39-08:00","id":420621,"title":"","content":"I imagine a lamprey host ziir werewolf would make an interesting opponent too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T18:37:14-08:00","id":420958,"title":"","content":"Probably like a giant lamprey with an insatiable blood lust.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T23:59:22-08:00","id":421402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/419096-ukusgualu-the-lamprey-hosts?p=419633#post419633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I brained them up for my Paris game. I'd have loved to have hinted at Lamprey Hosts in the core if I'd had the space, but since I didn't, here you go <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Coincidentally, a Lamprey Host comes up in Lodges: the Splintered, in the Lodge of Songkran writeup. They're not the same as this write-up - they're called the Kha-Yaawk, and they're described as being solitary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T03:52:59-08:00","id":421561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doctor Crimson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/419096-ukusgualu-the-lamprey-hosts?p=420530#post420530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was Ukusgualu like before it was shattered into the many shards that composes the Host?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm mulling over that at the moment. Due to their link with tides etc, I'm considering that their progenitor may have been a child of Luna, or even a royal avatar of Luna gone rogue <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/419096-ukusgualu-the-lamprey-hosts?p=421402#post421402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Coincidentally, a Lamprey Host comes up in Lodges: the Splintered, in the Lodge of Songkran writeup. They're not the same as this write-up - they're called the Kha-Yaawk, and they're described as being solitary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, been a while since I last read Splintered so I missed that!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T06:24:59-08:00","id":421680,"title":"","content":"Yours are a lot better anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T07:13:59-08:00","id":421725,"title":"","content":"I've think that the Host from Splintered were Leech, not Lamprey (which may or may not be considered &quot;close enough&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T07:24:11-08:00","id":421735,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I went and had a look and they're Leech Hosts in Splintered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T09:40:59-08:00","id":421890,"title":"","content":"I am curious, are you the same Acrozatarim that wrote and GMed the Warhammer Fantasy game &quot;The Shadow Of The Sun&quot;? If so, that was an amazing game and read.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?421186-Warhammer-Fantasy-2e-The-Shadow-Of-The-Sun\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...dow-Of-The-Sun</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3412-doctor-crimson","name":"Doctor Crimson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T10:15:47-08:00","id":421919,"title":"","content":"Once long ago, there lived a lamprey-spirit by the name of Little Worm; it swam the sea of Pangaea, latching onto spirit and flesh alike, and it was good. To be honest, Little Worm was barely aware of itself; all it knew was the warm embrace of the waters and the warm taste of Essence-rich blood pouring into its gullet.<br /> <br /> But one day (a day like many other days), a great spirit, Father Wolf, came to drink in a Locus it had called its own. Obeying its nature, it wriggled and writhed and drove itself inside the great hunter's spirit-flesh, sinking fangs into his great veins and drinking deep. And so Little Worm grew, and hungered more, and sipped upon Father Wolf's Essence, becoming Magath, an unclean mix of hunter and parasite.<br /> <br /> Oh how the Wolf-Spirit howled and raged in pain! Oh how he clawed his own flesh, tore at his own gizzard, shredded his limbs! Until three days and three nights later, when Mad Luna hung high in the sky, he found Little Worm, grown to the size of a tree. He tore it free, and dashed it against the rocks at his feet, watching it wriggle and writhe and break into a thousand thousand pieces, lampreys all.<br /> <br /> And so the Ukusgaulu, the Red-Paste Fish, came into this sorry world. How do I know?<br /> <br /> This story is true, child.<br /> <br /> (Sorry, I couldn't help myself.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T16:30:22-08:00","id":422298,"title":"","content":"Amechra, that's actually pretty interesting; I'll likely use it as one of the versions that the Hunters in Darkness try to explain the <i>Ukusgualu </i>with.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, my hapless players encountered an infested werewolf and later an actual <i>Ukusgualu</i> in today's session. It was a lot of fun, especially since the ithaeur was convinced it <i>had</i> to be some sort of spirit at work and was unconvinced by the Host indications for some time - because, well, no rats or spiders were involved <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T13:02:47-08:00","id":423341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> IT JUST GOT WORSE </div> </div> </div>Wait! there is still the issue about the eldritch god abomination attracted to the alienated humans near the infected gauntlet and their bloody rites, which is considered weird even for the Lampreys.<br /> It can be <b>even</b> worse","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T13:08:00-08:00","id":423348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/419096-ukusgualu-the-lamprey-hosts?p=421561#post421561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm mulling over that at the moment. Due to their link with tides etc, I'm considering that their progenitor may have been a child of Luna, or even a royal avatar of Luna gone rogue <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> And that's assuming that their progenitor is dead rather than somehow, say, spliting itself into hundreds of thousands of pieces in order to let some sort of THING in as part of a deal or something, remaining alive but in the background of his &quot;children's&quot; minds. <br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm probably not going to sleep tonight, so good job!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T18:09:15-08:00","id":423645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/419096-ukusgualu-the-lamprey-hosts?p=423348#post423348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And that's assuming that their progenitor is dead rather than somehow, say, spliting itself into hundreds of thousands of pieces in order to let some sort of THING in as part of a deal or something, remaining alive but in the background of his &quot;children's&quot; minds.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm probably not going to sleep tonight, so good job!</div> </div> </div> </div>This, I liked the hint in Wolfsbane that the swarm-Idigam might be the progenitor of the Locust Hosts. Might do something horrible like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T18:33:53-08:00","id":423665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/419096-ukusgualu-the-lamprey-hosts?p=423645#post423645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This, I liked the hint in Wolfsbane that the swarm-Idigam might be the progenitor of the Locust Hosts. Might do something horrible like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth pointing out it's a little ambiguous (by way of divergent statements on the opposite pages) whether the Srizaku are supposedly the children of He-Who-Consumes or the fragments of one of his brood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T19:38:45-08:00","id":423715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doctor Crimson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/419096-ukusgualu-the-lamprey-hosts?p=421890#post421890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am curious, are you the same Acrozatarim that wrote and GMed the Warhammer Fantasy game &quot;The Shadow Of The Sun&quot;? If so, that was an amazing game and read.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?421186-Warhammer-Fantasy-2e-The-Shadow-Of-The-Sun\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...dow-Of-The-Sun</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Missed this first time!<br /> <br /> Yes, that's me. One day I will get round to finishing the write-up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T20:43:30-08:00","id":423768,"title":"","content":"So while we're waiting for Werewolf 2nd to be released for the juicy, juicy mechanics. Care to indulge (some?) of us at how these guys would interact with Vampires. I've always like to see the intersection of two predators hunting the same food source. However, this one has the juicy question of 'So, infected vampires, eh? Those gotta be pretty.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T04:00:37-08:00","id":423951,"title":"","content":"Horrifying, awesome Host for a game. Really nice job, Acrozatarim. Like Raistlin, i'm also very interested on those alien godly abomination that gets summoned when the hybrids construct their pyramids. I think i will have this introduced in my currently Call of Cthulhu game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T05:54:10-08:00","id":424033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/419096-ukusgualu-the-lamprey-hosts?p=423768#post423768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while we're waiting for Werewolf 2nd to be released for the juicy, juicy mechanics. Care to indulge (some?) of us at how these guys would interact with Vampires. I've always like to see the intersection of two predators hunting the same food source. However, this one has the juicy question of 'So, infected vampires, eh? Those gotta be pretty.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh wow, yes. Well, for starters I now want to do a Jiang Shi write-up-style of a group of vampires that are Lamprey Hosts gravitating towards the communal vampire state that the various Clans share.<br /> <br /> Setting that aside, though, Christ, <i>Ukusgualu</i> and vampires interacting would be interesting. Obviously a fair amount depends on the relative balance of strength between the Lampreys and the Kindred in an area, but I think we can take certain things as a given. An example of how things might play out:<br /> <br /> You're a vampire. You've been reborn into undeath, a walking cadaver sustained by the blood and the Beast. You've become part of the All-Night Society, the community of vampires in your city, and are enmeshed in their power plays, their politics and their mysteries. One day, someone starts 'poaching' on your feeding grounds. People are being fed off, and it's both taking from <i>your</i> meal and threatening problems from investigations - the vampires, whoever they are, are a mix of clean and messy feeders. Some are leaving little more than pinpricks on their victims, but others leave messy throat scars - if they even feed from the throat rather than another body part. Sometimes the wounds are becoming properly infected. The victims seem to be delirious afterwards, at least, and have little memory of what happened to them, but their poor health and the sickness that plagues them is screwing with <i>your</i> herd. You pull some strings; whoever this is hasn't cleared their depredations with the high-ups, and none of the Covenants are willing to take the blame. If you're lucky, maybe you have access to some allies with lore and you do some research. You wonder whether a rogue bloodline has taken your turf as a playground. A few worrying names start to bubble up amongst those who learn of what's going on - some wonder if the Morbus are at work.<br /> <br /> You corner one of the intruders in a back-alley where they've lured a hapless victim to. In you swagger, all ready to show them who's boss, and it all goes wrong immediately. They aren't normal Kindred; your Beast flinches back from the revulsive sense of <i>other</i> you get from the man-shaped horror. It opens its mouth and there are far too many fangs in there. Still, the thing isn't particularly <i>strong</i>, and you and your allies tear it apart. It erupts in a tidal wave of squirming eel-things that go writhing away into the shadows, leaving just a hollowed out pile of wet skin and bloody bones. Someone gets bitten by one of them in the chaos. It's disgusting, but one thing is clear - these Kindred are something completely unlike any of the Clans or Bloodlines you've heard of.<br /> <br /> Things get worse. More of the Lampreys start appearing and feeding. They stage an ambush; a vampire you know is grabbed and never seen again. The south half of what is supposed to be <i>your</i> territory is becoming a no-go zone because it's near the river, and everyone is terrified that's where the infection has started - some sort of blood-drinking lampreys in the water. If you go there, the smell of blood is always in your face, maddening and tantalising. Sometimes you can see it just <i>dripping</i> out of no-where in corners, here and there. Your ghoul, hungry on a bad day, tried some of the blood. Now she's gone rogue and started some sort of bizarre cult amongst the riverside humans. Now <i>she</i> is leading them in trying to kidnap vampires she knows of so that the cult can feed from them. She's tried targeting you, but you've moved your haven to somewhere high, somewhere dry, somewhere with a <i>lot</i> of padlocks and where there are no vents or drains that the lampreys can get through.<br /> <br /> The rest of the city can't ignore the Lamprey Bloodline any more. They've gone from a bizarre and horrifying curiosity to a real threat, because other Kindred's territories butt onto the river too. They regularly attack vampires they encounter now, but they aren't killing them - Kindred are drunk from and then set free. High-rankers in the Covenants are forced to do something by the clamouring lower rankers. Organised attacks are launched; it's time to go into the docklands and clear these things out. Ghouls are to go in during the day; the Kindred will then move in at night.<br /> <br /> When nightfall comes, you get to hear the garbled reports from the surviving ghouls. Most of the Lampreys can walk under the sun and need not sleep. They may prefer the night, but they are by no means bound to it. Attacks on Lamprey 'nests' have had mixed success, with heavy casualties on both sides; a blood-drunk ghoul is a good match for a bag of skin and bones stuffed with lampreys, but some of the monsters are showing new and disturbing capabilities, and their bodies have started to warp and mutate further. Some ghouls just disappeared. Others never came back but left jumbled messages talking about the blood between worlds, and that they must swim the divide.<br /> <br /> The Kindred taking part in the attack go in. It's as bad as you fear, and the blood, the blood everywhere. The river water seems to <i>stink</i> of it - a human would barely notice it but your Beast growls with ravenous hunger. Pressed and on the back foot, the Lampreys fight hard; they're no match for angry vampires, but it's not just them that you're facing now. The lampreys themselves come squirming out of pipes, out of vents, out of drains, biting into panicking Kindred who tear them off and stamp the things to jelly underfoot. Some start to scream and claw at their own skin as bloody pock-marks appear, shouting about unseen leeches clamping onto them that they cannot get off. One Kindred sends himself to Final Death in a frenzy of self-mutilation. You feel something clamp onto your back, feel an oozing wound, but <i>there's nothing there</i>. More of the Kindred start to frenzy as some otherworldly presence drinks deep of their Vitae.<br /> <br /> Then the Lamprey elders appear. Slick-skinned worm-men, their bodies androgynous, their faces writhing circles of teeth and hunger, and they're <i>fast</i>. These things <i>are</i> a match for the Kindred who still stand, their spindly limbs possessing immense strength. Some spray blinding gouts of ichorous blood from their mouths; others literally fall apart into pools of bloody water, only to reform elsewhere. Something even bigger wallows beneath the warehouse floor; a massive lamprey-thing that smashes its way upwards, the progenitor of these horrors perhaps. Its immense bulk alone is enough to flatten one hapless lick.<br /> <br /> Carnage and blood and lampreys everywhere. Even these elders erupt into writhing eels when they're killed. And despite the horrors, you <i>are winning</i>. Whatever twisted power of the blood these things possess, you have your own strengths and your own elders. Powerful old Kindred feel threatened enough by what is happening to join the fray.<br /> <br /> You win. <i>You win</i>.<br /> <br /> The ghouls set several buildings on fire as the Kindred retreat, and the news that morning is rife with stories of gangland warfare and arson.<br /> <br /> And then it gets worse.<br /> <br /> You've won, but it'll take time to rebuild; the blood-mad humans and your rogue ghoul are still out there, plus any survivors of the Lamprey Bloodline. You get together with other Kindred of your level of society who share riverside territory, and start to plan a systematic method of clearing up - the high-ups have thrown the responsibility down on the shoulders of you Ancillae. Half-way through the meeting, one of the Kindred starts to cough and gag. He vomits. Amidst the blood on the table writhes a lamprey.<br /> <br /> You all stare.<br /> <br /> He's one of those who was bitten in the struggle. Paranoia explodes around that table and quickly spreads further on the medium of frantic phonecalls. Suddenly everyone who was bitten is a suspect, but no-one's quite sure of <i>what.</i> Are they infected somehow? Disease carriers? What happens next?<br /> <br /> The knives come out. High-ups have bitten vampires isolated where possible. Some escape the round-up; some conceal the fact they were bitten; some <i>are</i> high-ups, and who is going to try and incarcerate one of the elders? The Ordo are eager to get their hands on subjects to test and observe.<br /> <br /> The next night, you meet another Ancillae in your territory near the waterfront. He shouldn't be hear. You challenge him angrily, and he opens his mouth, and it is full of lampreys.<br /> <div align=\"center\">* * *</div> <br /> In the end, a frail accord is brought about. Only some of the infected Kindred are turned into Lampreys over the following days, and no-one can understand the whys and wherefores of who ends up hollowed out and who doesn't. Once a bloody purge is done, the Lampreys surprise everyone by making contact through a ghoul of some sort. The water-vampires lay out the obvious; this struggle has been pricy for both sides, but the Kindred have evidently failed to defeat them, and further attacks will simply cost more Kindred with the same result. Equally, the Lampreys are apparently only interested in the riverside territories. They apologise - <i>apologise!</i> - for the violence and attacks, calling them a 'misunderstanding', but now that they understand the Kindred they feel there is no need for further struggle. If the Kindred wisely cede the riverside territories to the Lampreys, the Lampreys will co-exist in peace, and will even send representatives to the Prince's court in deference to Kindred authority to shoulder the responsibility for what happens along the river.<br /> <br /> With bile in their throats, the Kindred agree. No-one is sure how the Lampreys infect Kindred after a bite, but one of the elders who was bitten has disappeared and there are once again numerous men and women packed full of Lampreys on the waterfront Rack, as if the whole battle never happened. The vampires will need time to understand these things if any further clash will be anything other than futile. Too many Kindred have met Final Death already, and there's no guarantee the remaining vampires can <i>win</i> a fight against an enemy they don't seem able to actually kill permanently. Over the enraged objections of those who have riverside territories, the accord is signed.<br /> <br /> The Kindred loathe them still, of course, even as they start to weave the Lampreys into their schemes. Everyone looks on the two pallid representatives to the Prince's court with disgust, watches in horror at the shivering and writhing beneath their skin, but they still <i>talk</i> to them. The Lampreys, it seems, have their own internal struggles, their own agendas and factions. They seem to want to eat each <i>other</i> far more than they want to kill Kindred. Things settle down over time; theoretically everyone's supposed to be figuring out the weaknesses of the Lampreys but the Horrible New becomes the Status Quo. The Ordo Dracul are rumoured to have captured Lampreys and dissected them behind closed doors. The Crone are rumoured to have cosied up to the fish-vampires, and there are even scurrilous whispers that some have voluntarily become infested with them in bloody old rites that the Circle guards jealously. A few angry Kindred who have lost their territories try to move againt the Lampreys; they're sometimes seen later, mad-eyed and blood-hungry, their bodies bulging with squirming parasites, and soon burn themselves out in ravenous frenzy. At least one Kindred, bitten in a scuffle by a Lamprey over a particular bit of territory border, decides to walk into the sunrise rather than... whatever it is that happens next to the bitten.<br /> <br /> No-one talks about the blood-cults around the river, or the way everything seems to taste and smell of blood to the Kindred. As long as the Lampreys keep control of it, as long as they keep everything nice and orderly, Kindred would rather not have to think about it. And that's what the Lampreys do, for a while.<br /> <br /> Then, years later, a new Lamprey representative turns up at the court. It has a petition for new territory, away from the river, in an area of the city that used to be a marsh. There are strong hints that if the petition is refused, the Lampreys will take it by force. And now there are new reports of vampire feeding grounds near the Lampreys' existing turf; that same bloody touch to the very air itself has spread. Blood is starting to trickle out of no-where, and <i>things</i> wallow in the sewers. The Lampreys are testing the will of the Kindred, seeing how far they can push them for more concessions.<br /> <br /> No-one is sure what happens next, not even the Lampreys.<br /> <div align=\"center\">* * *</div> <br /> And then there's you.<br /> <br /> You spent the night in the bath, your flesh carefully sliced open, blood everywhere, as you pulled the writhing worm-fish from your flesh. Mad with the pain and the gore, you made sure every last lamprey was torn apart before you smashed the bath itself to pieces and spent 'til morning screaming til your throat was raw and bloody.<br /> <br /> You've drunk the blood that pools where the Lampreys lair. You've walked like a shadow amongst them and, while the parasites know <i>someone is there</i> the Disciplines of your blood have kept you just a hair's breadth ahead of them so far. You've heard the whispers that the humans unwillingly mutter amongst themselves when they studiously ignore a drop of blood on a windowpane, and the incomprehending chants of cultists clustered round a pyramid of wet brass and bone in a basement.<br /> <br /> You've started to see the deeper well of blood everywhere; the shore of red that washes up against reality, with lampreys sporting and squirming in its shallows. You've seen people with lampreys clustered across their skin, drinking deep, even though they can't see the parasites themselves because the horrors are half-submerged in the sea of blood. You've heard the crashing roar of the waves, and beneath that something else, the heartbeat of something vast and great that wants to reach out, to speak to you.<br /> <br /> You have a plan. If you can catch one of the elders, the ghastly man-lamprey hybrids, when it is weak or vulnerable or utterly unwary, and snare it - if rather than 'killing' it and letting it turn into a thousand lampreys, you can drink down its blood, all of it, to the last drop, and truly diablerise it...<br /> <br /> ... Then perhaps you too can step onto that shore, and swim in the ocean of blood. Perhaps from the secrets in the Vitae of the lamprey, you can find the gateway to that paradise-nightmare, and forever sport amidst the crimson waves and rejoice and laugh and kill. And perhaps you can hear the whispers of what lies beneath, the vast and ancient heartbeat of that ocean.<br /> <br /> First, you must hunt, and kill, and drink.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T06:28:54-08:00","id":424066,"title":"","content":".... And ONCE AGAIN, I will not be sleeping tonight. Great job! Now, if anyone needs me, I'll just be avoiding all bodies of water out of paranoid fear!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T06:57:16-08:00","id":424094,"title":"","content":"Wow.<br /> That. Was. Awesome.<br /> <br /> Well done! Introduced like this, they seem as almost a better enemy for the vampires than the werewolves. For the weres they are just another host, although a creepy one, for the vampires they are rivals.<br /> <br /> A question, can the Lampreys reproduce given enough Essence, like the Spiders can, or do they have to attract more eels from other places?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:19:28-08:00","id":424127,"title":"","content":"oh god why<br /> <br /> (Thank you that was brilliant.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:22:18-08:00","id":424134,"title":"","content":"Hum. Vague notions of how to do a Jiang Shi style Clan write-up for whatever godawful hybrid fusion comes out of vampires feeding off <i>Ukusgualu</i> and vice versa.<br /> <br /> For Clan Disciplines I'd assume at least one of the physical Disciplines, maybe two. Resilience and Celerity maybe. Both Protean and Nightmare would be suitable, but are both the 'trademark' Disciplines for other Clans, so I'll say no to those but assume it's pretty common for the Lamprey-spawned Clan-In-The-Making to pick them up. Then a unique Clan Discipline relating to the Gauntlet, letting them do weird shit and giving them a closer tie to the Shadow than most vampires.<br /> <br /> What of the Clan Weakness? Could be something relating to water and needing dampness etc or they dry out and wither away, or could be something else freakishly weird involving lampreys, lampreys everywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:26:17-08:00","id":424140,"title":"","content":"I would say go with something related to needing dampness so that the clan weakness enforces things like territorial preferences and other common behaviors/stereotypes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:27:00-08:00","id":424141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/419096-ukusgualu-the-lamprey-hosts?p=424134#post424134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hum. Vague notions of how to do a Jiang Shi style Clan write-up for whatever godawful hybrid fusion comes out of vampires feeding off <i>Ukusgualu</i> and vice versa.<br /> <br /> For Clan Disciplines I'd assume at least one of the physical Disciplines, maybe two. Resilience and Celerity maybe. Both Protean and Nightmare would be suitable, but are both the 'trademark' Disciplines for other Clans, so I'll say no to those but assume it's pretty common for the Lamprey-spawned Clan-In-The-Making to pick them up. Then a unique Clan Discipline relating to the Gauntlet, letting them do weird shit and giving them a closer tie to the Shadow than most vampires.<br /> <br /> What of the Clan Weakness? Could be something relating to water and needing dampness etc or they dry out and wither away, or could be something else freakishly weird involving lampreys, lampreys everywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't this be more suited as a Bloodline? One that &quot;infects&quot; vampires who feed on the Ukusgualu, perhaps. That could give them a weird Bloodline-blessing that affects the Gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T12:55:27-08:00","id":424394,"title":"","content":"That was really damn great. If there is one thing that will get the Uratha and Kindred working together, it's that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:09:34-08:00","id":424414,"title":"","content":"That is excellent.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">L</span>amprey-<span style=\"font-size:16px\">K</span>indred</span><br /> Disciplines:</b> <i>Bloodtide</i>, Celerity, Resilience<br /> <b>Clan Bane:</b> The Lampreys are <i>infested</i> with their namesakes; they swarm under their skin, spill from their mouths and leave bloody kisses over their skin. What's worse, their paper-dry skin needs to be kept moist; when dry, they take damage as if they were exposed to sunlight, except they downgrade any damage they would take by one step.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:17:27-08:00","id":424419,"title":"","content":"So how long before they are dried out, and begin to take damage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:23:46-08:00","id":424425,"title":"","content":"Depends on the climate; I've lived in places where stuff dries in a few minutes and others where stuff stays damp for<i> days</i>. I really wouldn't be comfortable assigning a specific time range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T23:51:54-08:00","id":424922,"title":"","content":"Theoretically, if the cycle went on long enough they would eventually gain Humanity as they grew closer to Kindredom. Thnk about how weird THAT would be.<br /> <br /> <i>Your a happy little </i><i>Ukusgualu, and things have been pretty great so far. You've eaten plenty of your siblings and started to become a happy <b>big</b> Ukusgualu, plus the world is nice and slippery, so there's always a lot of tasty blood to be had (especially tasty when it comes out of one of those cold guys). Some things haven't been so great though, for example: being out in the Sun makes you feel so sleepy, and worst of all, </i><b><i>it</i></b><i><b> hurts</b></i><i>. Most of your other siblings don't seem to have that problem, so why do you? None of that really matters right now though because you just discovered that humans have a delicious shard inside of them. It's bigger then any of your siblings were and you've already eaten a lot of blood, but it's just so good you can't help but burrow in deeper to get more! You suck, and suck, and suck until...<br /> <br /> What the hell was that!? Who is Maddy and what is love and why do you suddenly have an opinion on the newest Transformers movie (it sucked)?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","user":"Xenorath","date":". 03-02-2015, 02:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T02:42:32-08:00","id":424979,"title":"","content":"More and more awesomeness showing in the thread :3 Give us that Lamprey Bloodline, giiiiiive us!!! It could have an adaptation of the Spirit Discipline that allowed vampires to go trough the gauntlet, i wonder?How would be maintained the equilibrium between the vampire and the lampreys inside? Or it wouldn't be an equilibrium?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T04:05:57-08:00","id":424994,"title":"","content":"I think I'll probably run the Bane as being that they need to rest in water when they torpor during the day, or else they suffer damage/debuffs the next day; then make it a sliding scale of the restrictions they suffer depending on diminishing Humanity. A Humanity 6 Lamprey Kindred can just fill the bath and get in; a Humanity 4 needs to actually sleep in a river or lake or pond, a natural source of water; Humanity 1 needs it to be nice and bloody; that sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T10:06:45-08:00","id":431383,"title":"","content":"I guess I should start working on the Dread Powers for the <i>Ukusgualu</i> and maybe stat some sample ones up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Not sure whether to call their signature power Liquefy Gauntlet, Taint Gauntlet, Crimson Gauntlet or something else <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T11:06:20-08:00","id":431510,"title":"","content":"Awesome! I think Liquefy Gauntlet makes the most sense to me for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T17:19:23-08:00","id":432020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/419096-ukusgualu-the-lamprey-hosts?p=431383#post431383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I should start working on the Dread Powers for the <i>Ukusgualu</i> and maybe stat some sample ones up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Not sure whether to call their signature power Liquefy Gauntlet, Taint Gauntlet, Crimson Gauntlet or something else <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Bleeding Gauntlet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T18:25:22-08:00","id":432090,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure it isn't actually a word, but maybe Insanguinate Gauntlet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T05:35:00-07:00","id":432550,"title":"","content":"Sanguine Gauntlet might work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T06:29:44-07:00","id":433881,"title":"","content":"Initial drafts of a couple of Dread Powers for the Lamprey Hosts:<br /> <br /> <b>Liquefy Gauntlet (<i>Ukusgualu</i> only)</b><br /> With an hour of constant work, costing 1 Essence acquired through drinking blood in the process, an <i>Ukusgualu</i> can regurgitate blood into the Gauntlet and cause it to start taking on a fluid state. This shifts the Gauntlet strength up by one if less than 2 and down by one if more than 2. This affects an area of 10 square yards. The Gauntlet takes on a bloodied state, and any attempt to use senses to perceive the other side of the Gauntlet will be affected as such; vision is red and bloodied, nostrils are filled with the stench of gore, and the taste is like an abbatoir. When the senses are returned to their normal state, the character finds that blood has come back with them; looking across the Gauntlet leaves blood dripping from their eyes, for example. Anyone who attempts to perceive across the Gauntlet in a liquefied area must pass a Resolve + Composure roll or suffer an Integrity or Wisdom breaking point, or a breaking point towards Spirit.<br /> <br /> <b>Swim Gauntlet (<i>Ukusgualu </i>only)</b><br /> By spending 2 Essence, an <i>Ukusgualu</i> can dive into the Gauntlet in any area where Liquefy Gauntlet has been used to shift its strength to 2 (even if the strength was originally 2, Liquefy Gauntlet must still have been used). This is a similar process to crossing over the Gauntlet, except no Locus is needed and the <i>Ukusgualu</i> ends up wrapped in the Gauntlet itself. The <i>Ukusgualu</i> can move around within the Gauntlet and can emerge from it to attack, with the same effects as if it used the Gauntlet Cloak power.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T07:17:46-07:00","id":433958,"title":"","content":"Are you sticking all this stuff in your wiki somewhere? I'd like to use it, but I don't want to cut and paste it into my wiki. I'd much prefer to stick a link in to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T17:41:17-07:00","id":448532,"title":"","content":"The mention of blood dripping through and making people want to build strange monuments makes me think of the Forbidden Siren franchise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T17:47:19-07:00","id":448536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/419096-ukusgualu-the-lamprey-hosts?p=419330#post419330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may be the most horrifying monster I have ever read about for the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes you want to hide your kids and hide your wife.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T05:57:14-07:00","id":449056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/419096-ukusgualu-the-lamprey-hosts?p=433958#post433958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sticking all this stuff in your wiki somewhere? I'd like to use it, but I don't want to cut and paste it into my wiki. I'd much prefer to stick a link in to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not putting it up atm, no - if nothing else, the bit on the rpg.net wiki we use for our game is a place that my players look at and I don't want them getting the full down-low on what the <i>Ukusgualu</i> are capable of <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If you want to link to it here, go ahead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laraqua</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/419096-ukusgualu-the-lamprey-hosts?p=448532#post448532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mention of blood dripping through and making people want to build strange monuments makes me think of the Forbidden Siren franchise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not familiar with that franchise. A quick Google Search indicates it's a series of games that sound kinda Silent Hill-ish?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T20:46:34-07:00","id":562557,"title":"","content":"Still interested to hear about their motivation. The teaser about tides and the sun and moon was tantalizing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T14:30:12-07:00","id":594141,"title":"","content":"I'm not a huge fan of <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken</b> (well, not yet... I'm still digesting Second Edition), but this is some really neat and spooky-as-hell stuff! Thanks mate; you made me afraid of water in a way that <i>Jaws</i> never did. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T02:30:27-07:00","id":599101,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking about Lamprey Hosts again because of an idea I had for a city, and the more I think about them the more I think they might be my favorite Host. For the record, Locusts used to be my favorite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T20:09:15-07:00","id":604438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/419096-ukusgualu-the-lamprey-hosts?p=562557#post562557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still interested to hear about their motivation. The teaser about tides and the sun and moon was tantalizing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd like to second the desire to hear more about their Motivation. Also possibly mechanics if they've been perfected! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I've got a Werewolf game coming up and would love to use the Lamprey's in it! Also they'd make a fun guest star/rumour for my currently going on Vampire game!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T01:35:40-07:00","id":604552,"title":"","content":"I'll have a crack at something once I'v